    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Northern Arapaho Tribe of Wyoming originally occupied the headwaters of the Arkansas and Platte Rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://northernarapaho.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Northern Arapaho people speak a variation of the Algonquin language and are the most southwest extension of those people.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://northernarapaho.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A Catholic mission was founded in Arapahoe in 1884, which includes the nearby St. Stephen's Mission Church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arapahoe%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Northern Arapaho were placed on the Wind River Reservation after the Treaty of 1868 left them without a land base.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://northernarapaho.com/"
    },
    {
